We need to perform three sequential high-quality scans of same 10x10 µm² area, points per line 128, lines per frame 128, set time per line such that all three scans completed within 2 min 34 s (i.e., 154 seconds). So each scan time = 154/3 ≈ 51.33 s. Time per line = total scan time / lines per frame. So time per line ≈ 51.33 / 128 ≈ 0.401 s per line (401 ms). Need scanning mode that minimizes tip damage: likely "Tapping mode" or "Non-contact". Use "Tapping" (also called "AC mode") which reduces tip wear. We'll need to set scanning mode accordingly.

We need to collect topographic data and calculate RMS roughness for each scan. Use Image_Analyzer with calculate_rms_roughness=True.

We need to run scans via AFM API. Likely need code to initialize AFM, set scan parameters, start scan, save image. Use Document_Retrieval to get code snippets for initializing, setting scan parameters, setting mode, starting scan, saving.

First retrieve code for initializing AFM and loading application.
Let's retrieve relevant snippets.
{
    "tool_name": "Document_Retrieval",
    "arguments": {
        "query": "initialize AFM and load application nanosurf python"
    }
}
